<title>SWEDEN: SSAB 1996 profit plunges 45 pct.</title>
<headline>SSAB 1996 profit plunges 45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Earnings for Swedish steel group SSAB in 1996, reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 2,091  vs 3,832</p>
<p> Sales				     17,408  vs 19,004</p>
<p> Earnings per share (crowns)	  11.60  vs 21.30</p>
<p> Proposed dividend (crowns)	    4.00  vs  4.00</p>
<p> Operating costs			 15,002  vs 14,833</p>
<p> Depreciation				 750  vs    690</p>
<p> Operating profit			 1,656  vs  3,481</p>
<p> Shares in associated companies	  81  vs     97</p>
<p> Financial net				354  vs    254</p>
<p> Minorities			  CHARGE  47  vs     73 CHARGE</p>
<p>NOTE -- A Reuters poll of 13 analysts showed expectations for profit after financial items averaged 1.98 billion crowns for calendar 1996.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
